          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "During their walk in the forests, Bhoomi and Surya notice that there are a lot of leaves on the ground and the soil feels damp. Ajji explains, “The roots of plants hold on to the soil and prevent it from being washed away. The leaves that fall from the trees decay and enrich the soil with nutrients. This soil is used by new plants and trees to grow. This is an example of recycling in nature.” Let us investigate the soil in more detail."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
